      "worked": "Draw $Ab$ and $aB$ and label their intersection $X$. Draw $Ac$ and $aC$ and label their intersection $Y$. Draw $Bc$ and $bC$ and label their intersection $Z$. The three intersections lie on one straight line, as stated by Pappus’s Hexagon Theorem.",
